<title>TURKEY: Turkey's wheat imports may rise to 2 mln T in 1996.</title>
<headline>Turkey's wheat imports may rise to 2 mln T in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's wheat imports, mainly by private millers, may reach two million tonnes this calendar year, compared with 1.246 million imported in 1995, Agriculture Minister Musa Demirci said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;This is one of the highest import figures in recent years despite a rise in wheat output by 500,000 tonnes,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Demirci said imports had reached 1.35 million tonnes by the end of September.</p>
<p>He reiterated earlier estimates of domestic output of 18.5 million tonnes in 1996/97.</p>
<p>But Western traders and analysts said Turkey's wheat output would not exceed 16.5 million tonnes in 1996/97, up from 15.5 million a year ago.</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
